{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Correction: the preceding one-word \"placeholder\" comment was posted in error\n\nThat comment was an accidental write from a lock-retry loop whose fallback path fired; it\ncarries no meaning and should be disregarded. The real attestation evidence is below.\n\n## [operator-attested] evidence — why this work is not codebase-discoverable, and the artifacts that prove it\n\nThe completion verifier correctly reported it could not confirm this work from the source\ntree. That is a **structural property of the task, not an unfinished repair**: the deliverable\nis a data repair to `.bridge_state/bindings.json` on the **`tickets` git branch**, plus\n**runtime `rebar bridge fsck` output**. There is deliberately no `src/` change (the plan's\nScope says so), and the tracker branch is not readable by codebase review tools — so a\n`grep REB-410` over the working tree correctly returns nothing. Every criterion is now tagged\n`[operator-attested]` per the gate's documented path, with artifacts below.\n\n### C1 — 13 reverse entries deleted; forward map and retired file unchanged\n\nCommitted diff on the tickets branch — one file, 13 pure deletions, zero additions:\n\n    .bridge_state/bindings.json | 13 -------------\n    1 file changed, 13 deletions(-)\n\n    -    \"REB-410\": \"b1c4-d00b-9212-4fa0\"      -    \"REB-417\": \"c652-360b-9169-4982\"\n    -    \"REB-411\": \"d53e-32bf-0d14-4c35\"      -    \"REB-418\": \"cb65-f0cb-8061-411c\"\n    -    \"REB-412\": \"f07e-84da-182d-4f96\"      -    \"REB-419\": \"eb3c-f55b-eacc-47b6\"\n    -    \"REB-413\": \"950e-79da-f99c-474e\"      -    \"REB-420\": \"3f93-084b-1d4d-4dfb\"\n    -    \"REB-414\": \"a220-e79d-f819-4e88\"      -    \"REB-421\": \"9e39-ef9f-3dc9-4e9a\"\n    -    \"REB-415\": \"ec6a-cc65-f236-4fa1\"      -    \"REB-422\": \"f4dd-b7dd-8307-4bea\"\n    -    \"REB-416\": \"94dc-264b-c6a4-41b5\"\n\nForward map unchanged: `bindings` = 2111 before and after. `bindings-retired.json`\nbyte-identical, sha256 `bd8c821923da2900ccde84d974ae18348f36ed30bb04e26cbef41f3ee31497b5`\non both sides. `get_rotation.json` untouched (absent from `git status`).\n\n### C2 / C5 — fsck store_integrity 13 -> 0, defect no longer reproduces\n\n`rebar bridge fsck --output json`, the same command that produced the original findings:\n\n    BEFORE                                  AFTER\n    store_integrity: 13                     store_integrity: 0   []\n    would_terminal=0  local_gone=0          would_terminal=0  local_gone=0\n    retired_overlap=0 dangling=0            retired_overlap=0 dangling=0\n    unbound_jira=0                          unbound_jira=0\n    unknown_event_types: 0                  unknown_event_types: 0\n\n(`absent_in_window_unprobed`=950 and `indeterminate`=5 are **non-alerting by design** —\n`_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:306` — and are unchanged by this repair.)\n\nDirect store read: `bindings`=2111 / `reverse`=2124 / 13 orphans **before**; `bindings`=2111 /\n`reverse`=2111 / **0 orphans** after. The ticket's own stated auto-close condition — \"zero\nalerting audit findings\" — is therefore met.\n\n### C3 — repaired through rebar's library, delivered by the sanctioned door, pushed\n\nSequence: `BindingStore` (`rebar_reconciler.binding_store`) -> delete the 13 orphaned\n`reverse` keys -> `BindingStore.save()` (tempfile + `os.replace`) ->\n`rebar._store.push.commit_and_push_tickets_branch(strict=True)`\n(`src/rebar/_store/push.py:639`), which commits under the store write lock and pushes.\n**No ad-hoc git in the tracker.** Four pre-write guards each aborted the write on failure\n(orphan set must equal exactly {REB-410...REB-422}; none retired; none holding a forward\nbinding; forward map unchanged and no orphan remaining post-deletion) — all passed.\n\nVerified **on the remote**, not merely locally —\n`git show origin/tickets:.bridge_state/bindings.json`: `bindings`=2111, `reverse`=2111,\norphans=0, `REB-410` absent from `reverse`. This check was load-bearing: the first push raced\na concurrent advance of `origin/tickets` (`cannot lock ref`) and rebar's auto-reconcile retry\nmerged it, and the tickets branch resolves `bindings.json` as `merge=ours`\n(`docs/concurrency.md:414`), so the merge outcome had to be confirmed rather than assumed.\nTracker is clean with 0 unpushed commits.\n\n### C4 — decision and evidence recorded\n\nThe operator's verbatim \"delete.\" decision was recorded **before** the repair; before/after\nevidence recorded after. Both are comments on this ticket.\n\n### Follow-up filed\n\nThe reverse-orphan leak class is filed as its own open, unclaimed bug —\n[rebar:874a-bda3-ee6f-45eb] (vinifera-farflung-nyala) — linked `discovered_from` this ticket."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786533338301756001,"uuid":"faa09632-bab4-4153-b05c-0e2f368b7f7e"}